    "result_text": "The full suite is just `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are an abstract base and a test helper). Everything is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the one place the code is built:\n- Now derives `CITY3` (upper-cased first 3 letters of city) and `LAST3` (first 3 of last name) via a shared `prefix()` helper.\n- `NNNN` is now a **per-city** sequence: one more than the number of existing owners already in that city, counted by iterating `findAll()` and matching city case-insensitively (`countInCity`) \u2014 mirroring the existing `CountNamesakes` pattern rather than adding a repository method or duplicating logic.\n\n**Everything derived from the code rebuilds automatically:** the membership number in `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber` is formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, so it inherits the new prefix with no logic change \u2014 I only refreshed its javadoc example (`SYD-SMI-0007-M26`).\n\n**Docs kept in sync:** updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` descriptions/examples in `openapi.yml`.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
